c since it was staging-only and unhealthy.)\n\n**What happened:**\n1. First rollback attempt partially failed \u2014 an orchestrator error halted it after us-east, leaving the fleet in a mixed state (us-east on v2.3.0, the other two still on v2.3.1).\n2. Retried the rollback; it completed successfully in all regions.\n3. Verified: all regions on v2.3.0, `healthy: true`, error rate down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api documenting the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the recovered state, and follow-ups. The create call timed out, but I confirmed via `list_incidents` that it was created exactly once \u2014 no duplicate page was sent.\n\n**Suggested follow-ups** (noted in the incident): root-cause v2.3.1 before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator error that interrupted the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}